    "functionName": "max_depth",
    "starterCode": "class TreeNode:\n    def __init__(self, value=0, left=None, right=None):\n        self.value = value\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\ndef max_depth(root):\n    # return the number of levels in the tree\n    ...\n",
    "prepareCode": "class TreeNode:\n    def __init__(self, value=0, left=None, right=None):\n        self.value = value\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\ndef build_tree(values):\n    if not values:\n        return None\n    root = TreeNode(values[0])\n    queue = [root]\n    i = 1\n    while queue and i < len(values):\n        node = queue.pop(0)\n        if i < len(values):\n            value = values[i]\n            i += 1\n            if value is not None:\n                node.left = TreeNode(value)\n                queue.append(node.left)\n        if i < len(values):\n            value = values[i]\n            i += 1\n            if value is not None:\n                node.right = TreeNode(value)\n                queue.append(node.right)\n    return root\n\ndef unlink_tree(node):\n    if node is None:\n        return\n    unlink_tree(node.left)\n    unlink_tree(node.right)\n    node.left = None\n    node.right = None\n\ndef prepare(raw):\n    root = build_tree(raw[0])\n    def finish(result):\n        unlink_tree(root)\n        return result\n    return [root], finish\n",
    "examples": [
      {
        "input": {
          "root": [
            5,
            3,
            8,
            1,
            null,
            7,
            9
          ]
        },
        "output": 3,
        "explanation": "The levels hold 5; then 3 and 8; then 1, 7, and 9."
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "root": [
            42
          ]
        },
        "output": 1,
        "explanation": "A single node makes one level."
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "The depth of a tree is one more than the deeper of its two subtrees.",
      "Every node belongs to exactly one root-to-leaf path, so one full walk can measure them all.",
      "Walk with a stack carrying (node, depth): track the deepest depth seen and push children one level deeper."
    ],
    "solution": "One traversal carrying each node’s depth: the answer is the deepest depth seen. O(n) time, O(depth) stack space.",
    "solutionCode": "def max_depth(root):\n    deepest = 0\n    stack = [(root, 1)] if root is not None else []\n    while stack:\n        node, depth = stack.pop()\n        if depth > deepest:\n            deepest = depth\n        if node.left is not None:\n            stack.append((node.left, depth + 1))\n        if node.right is not None:\n            stack.append((node.right, depth + 1))\n    return deepest\n",
    "bruteForceCode": "def max_depth(root):\n    def height(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return 0\n        return 1 + max(height(node.left), height(node.right))\n    best = 0\n    stack = [root] if root is not None else []\n    while stack:\n        node = stack.pop()\n        if node is None:\n            continue\n        measured = height(node)\n        if measured > best:\n            best = measured\n        stack.append(node.left)\n        stack.append(node.right)\n    return best\n",
    "failureHint": "hidden tests include an empty tree, a single node, and a lopsided tree",
