    "id": "02-longest-consecutive-sequence",
    "title": "Longest Consecutive Sequence",
    "track": "Hash Maps",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "topics": [
      "hash-maps",
      "arrays"
    ],
    "source": "canonical Longest Consecutive Sequence concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
    "description": "The input is an unsorted array of integers. Return the length of the longest run of consecutive values that can be assembled from its elements, in any order: values 4, 5, 6 form a run of length 3. Duplicates count once, and an empty array has a longest run of 0.",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= len(nums) <= 5000",
      "-1000000000 <= nums[i] <= 1000000000"
    ],
    "parameters": [
      "nums"
    ],
    "functionName": "longest_consecutive",
    "starterCode": "def longest_consecutive(nums):\n    # Return the length of the longest run of consecutive values.\n    ...\n",
    "examples": [
      {
        "input": {
          "nums": [
            12,
            4,
            200,
            2,
            3,
            1,
            5
          ]
        },
        "output": 5,
        "explanation": "The values 1 through 5 all appear, forming a consecutive run of 5."
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "nums": [
            7,
            2,
            9,
            4,
            1,
            6,
            2,
            8,
            5,
            3
          ]
        },
        "output": 9,
        "explanation": "Every value from 1 through 9 appears at least once, and the duplicate 2 counts once."
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Checking membership over and over is only cheap if the container answers in constant time.",
      "Put every value in a set. A value only needs checking when it is the start of a run, which is true exactly when value - 1 is absent.",
      "For each run start, walk value + 1, value + 2, ... while the set contains them, and track the longest walk. Only starting from run starts keeps the total work linear."
    ],
    "solution": "Load the values into a set for O(1) membership tests. Treat a value as a run start only when value - 1 is not in the set, then count upward while the next value exists. Every element is visited a constant number of times: O(n) time, O(n) space.",
    "solutionCode": "def longest_consecutive(nums):\n    values = set(nums)\n    best = 0\n    for value in values:\n        if value - 1 in values:\n            continue\n        length = 1\n        while value + length in values:\n            length += 1\n        if length > best:\n            best = length\n    return best\n",
    "bruteForceCode": "def longest_consecutive(nums):\n    best = 0\n    for value in nums:\n        if value - 1 in nums:\n            continue\n        length = 1\n        while value + length in nums:\n            length += 1\n        if length > best:\n            best = length\n    return best\n",
