    "hints": [
      "Cut the range at the midpoint: one side is still sorted, no matter the rotation.",
      "If nums[lo] <= nums[mid] the left half is sorted, so a quick range check says whether target can be there.",
      "Each step: identify the sorted half, test whether target lies inside it, and discard that half or the other one accordingly."
    ],
    "solution": "Modified binary search: at every midpoint, exactly one half is sorted; a range check against the sorted half decides whether to keep it or keep the other half. O(log n) time, O(1) space.",
    "solutionCode": "def search_rotated(nums, target):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(nums) - 1\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if nums[mid] == target:\n            return mid\n        if nums[lo] <= nums[mid]:\n            if nums[lo] <= target < nums[mid]:\n                hi = mid - 1\n            else:\n                lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            if nums[mid] < target <= nums[hi]:\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n    return -1\n",
    "bruteForceCode": "def search_rotated(nums, target):\n    for i, value in enumerate(nums):\n        if value == target:\n            return i\n    return -1\n",
